+# Isolated Eve UI fixture
+
+This uses the real Eve React component with stubbed child components and synthetic owner, history, runtime, and device responses. All application `fetch` calls are intercepted and other endpoints fail; no model is invoked. It is not a production account, a whole-site rendering, or Pixel device acceptance.
+
+From the Site source checkout, run `./node_modules/.bin/vite --config tests/fixtures/pixel-eve-ui/vite.config.mjs`. Open the printed loopback URL in a separate browser tab at 411 × 923 CSS pixels. Select Fixture A, click “次の応答を保留”, wait until “応答保留中”, then select Fixture B and Fixture A. Release the held response and verify that the current results remain unconfirmed until a new poll completes. Check “仕事と成果” after the poll. Reset the viewport, close only the test tab, and stop the owned Vite process afterwards. The fixture does not test a real account, saved work, actual phone, or the full production page styling.
+
+To test connection recovery, click “以前の会話を読む” to produce a synthetic operation error, hold the next response, and click “通信断を通知”. Release the held response and verify both the connection warning and operation error remain. Click “再接続を通知” and verify the warning clears after a successful poll while the operation error remains. “認証を失敗させる” and “認証を回復” simulate authentication loss and recovery; check that “仕事と成果” is disabled while signed out. “次の同期を失敗” simulates a transient sync failure. These controls alter only fixture state, not the device connection.
